Combine the data blocks ("ranges") of the RANGES sheet into the LISTS sheet.

How it works
------------
* Every range on RANGES is located dynamically: a range starts at a header row
  that contains "DATE" (column B) and "REF" (column C) - so newly added ranges
  are picked up automatically on every run.
* Inside each range, duplicates are matched on the DATE + REF pair (columns B
  and C) and their amounts are summed.
* The LISTS sheet is wiped in the answer region first (this deletes all the old
  ranges/sections) and is then repopulated section by section.  The layout of
  the already finished "STAGE" table (title row, header row, data rows, TOTAL
  row) is detected and used as the format reference for every section.
* Every section is sorted by DATE (lowest -> highest) with a secondary
  alphabetical (A -> Z) sort on column C (REF), and ends with a TOTAL row that
  sums the amounts.
* The result is saved to output.xlsx (a copy of input.xlsx), answer region
  A3:D32 of the LISTS sheet.
